sequenceDiagram
  participant C as Controller scheduler
  participant E as Evidence writer
  participant R as Resources and inspection worker
  Note over C: P0 validate, import, start writer. Nothing owned.
  C->>E: P1 setup frame: run name, plan, subjects
  E-->>C: Readiness with subject digests, within 5 s of spawn
  Note over C: P2 owned run starts. No controller filesystem call.
  C->>R: Start inspection worker
  loop Each resource n
    C->>E: intent-n frame
    E-->>C: intent-n acknowledgement, gate at most 2 s
    C->>R: Acquire resource n
  end
  C-)E: Call output, receipts, observations, fire and forget
  Note over C: Final drain of buffered output at each call's final observation, no wait for EOF
  C->>R: Cleanup, disposal, inspection, worker close
  Note over C: Teardown never waits for an acknowledgement
  Note over C: P3 publication starts at S, cutoff P = S + W, W at most 10 s
  C-)E: Ledger, subjects-after request
  E-->>C: Subjects-after digests, until S + W/2
  C-)E: Result snapshot, publication pending
  C-)E: Close frame
  Note over E: Close transaction: storage-close record, then identity over every file
  E-->>C: Close acknowledgement with storage-close and identity digests
  alt Writer acknowledges close before P
    C->>E: Exact-PID nonblocking reap by P + 2 s
  else Writer unfinished at P
    C->>E: KILL, then poll reap until P + 2 s
  end
  Note over C: Terminal outcome in memory by P + 2 s. An unreaped writer is a residual
